WEBVTT

00:00:04.590 --> 00:00:08.110
<i>Every time this season comes, 
I remember a certain scene.</i>

00:00:08.920 --> 00:00:13.890
<i>I used to love sneaking into the music
 room to play the grand piano.</i>

00:00:14.860 --> 00:00:16.990
<i>And on that day, I was doing just that...</i>

00:00:23.580 --> 00:00:26.300
<i>Back then, I didn't know anything.</i>

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:29.350
<i>Not that my father would 
pass away in a few years,</i>

00:00:29.350 --> 00:00:31.160
<i>or that I'd take over the company...</i>

00:00:32.060 --> 00:00:37.440
<i>Or that my father's life was taken by 
a mysterious organization, Black Swan.</i>

00:00:42.770 --> 00:00:51.440
"It takes all the running you can do, 
to keep in the same place."

00:00:42.770 --> 00:00:51.440
~The Red Queen Hypothesis~

00:00:53.360 --> 00:00:57.630
<i>In this world, there exist 
unique powers known as "Evol,"</i>

00:00:57.630 --> 00:00:59.870
<i>which are possessed by a very few.</i>

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:04.290
<i>Among them, some chose to fight 
their fate, to fight the world.</i>

00:01:04.290 --> 00:01:06.940
<i>This is the story of these young "Evolvers."</i>

00:02:22.410 --> 00:02:27.000
<b>Mr. Love: Queen's Choice</b>

00:02:27.250 --> 00:02:30.370
"An Amber Wind"

00:02:31.820 --> 00:02:34.560
A female student from Loveland 
High School has gone missing?

00:02:35.880 --> 00:02:39.510
<i>The mystery of Black Swan 
and my missing memories...</i>

00:02:39.510 --> 00:02:42.600
Name: <b><u>Anonyman</u></b>
I can't get a hold of her at all.
I thought she ran away, but would she leave her cell phone behind? 

00:02:39.790 --> 00:02:43.180
<i>I searched exhaustively, wondering 
if there might be any clues,</i>

00:02:43.180 --> 00:02:44.470
<i>and happened to find this.</i>

00:02:44.470 --> 00:02:46.930
<i>A small incident at my old high school.</i>

00:02:49.540 --> 00:02:50.210
<b>Kiro
</b>Morning

00:02:50.210 --> 00:02:54.110
but it's still too soon 
to push yourself!

00:02:50.210 --> 00:02:54.110
Got it. Thanks!

00:02:50.420 --> 00:02:54.110
Morning, Potato Chip Princess! 
You didn't stay up all night 
working again, did you? 
Though I'm not one to talk 
since I was up all night 
on location!

00:02:51.020 --> 00:02:52.760
<i>Morning, Potato Chip Princess!</i>

00:02:52.760 --> 00:02:54.610
<i>You didn't stay up all night 
working again, did you?</i>

00:02:54.610 --> 00:02:57.380
<i>Though I'm not one to talk since
 I was up all night on location!</i>

00:02:57.690 --> 00:02:59.650
Morning, Potato Chip Princess! 
You didn't stay up all night 
working again, did you? 
Though, I'm not one to talk 
since I was up all night 
on location!

00:02:57.840 --> 00:02:59.650
I'll keep looking into those 
guys, so don't worry about 
anything and just concentrate 
on your work, okay?

00:02:59.060 --> 00:03:02.320
<i>I'll keep looking into those guys,</i>

00:03:02.730 --> 00:03:06.400
<i>so don't worry about anything and 
just concentrate on your work, okay?</i>

00:03:08.250 --> 00:03:11.400
<i>Thanks. I'm doing fine.</i>

00:03:11.750 --> 00:03:13.030
<i>Send!</i>

00:03:11.750 --> 00:03:14.420
I'll keep looking into those 
guys, so don't worry about 
anything and just concentrate 
on your work, okay?

00:03:13.020 --> 00:03:14.420
Thanks.
 I'm doing fine!

00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:16.890
<i>Our latest episode of </i>Miracle Finder<i>,</i>

00:03:16.890 --> 00:03:20.380
<i>an exclusive interview with the 
legendary hacker, Key, was a big hit.</i>

00:03:20.780 --> 00:03:23.920
<i>Little by little, people are
 paying more attention to us.</i>

00:03:24.410 --> 00:03:27.940
<i>In the midst of all this, the idea Minor
 brought for our next segment was...</i>

00:03:28.770 --> 00:03:31.520
Segment Plan 
<i>"The Love Letter in the Desk"</i>

00:03:29.170 --> 00:03:31.520
"The Love Letter in the Desk"?

00:03:31.520 --> 00:03:32.990
Oh, I know what this is.

00:03:32.990 --> 00:03:34.720
That one movie that's all the rage.

00:03:34.720 --> 00:03:37.870
That's why letters are a big thing right now!

00:03:37.870 --> 00:03:40.610
That old-fashioned feeling seems
 fresh right now, you know?

00:03:40.610 --> 00:03:44.010
Which is why we should gather up a bunch 
of anecdotes centered around letters,

00:03:44.010 --> 00:03:46.280
and show the everyday, 
heartwarming miracles hidden in—

00:03:46.280 --> 00:03:47.790
So we ride the movie's popularity.

00:03:47.790 --> 00:03:49.680
Don't say it like that!

00:03:49.680 --> 00:03:51.160
It's obvious, though.

00:03:50.330 --> 00:03:51.500
<i>"The Love Letter in the Desk"</i>

00:03:51.160 --> 00:03:52.620
It's not like we're really riding it.

00:03:53.040 --> 00:03:54.780
How can you say that?

00:03:53.040 --> 00:03:55.720
<i>Honestly, I don't have any 
good memories about letters...</i>

00:03:55.720 --> 00:03:56.750
So, President!

00:03:56.750 --> 00:03:59.660
There was a ramen shop in
 front of our high school, right?

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:02.720
You think we could investigate 
the message board there?

00:04:03.500 --> 00:04:04.800
It's still there?

00:04:04.800 --> 00:04:06.930
According to my sources.

00:04:07.270 --> 00:04:10.740
And the rumor that if you confess your
 feelings there, they'll be reciprocated?

00:04:09.290 --> 00:04:12.230
Senpai, I love you.

00:04:09.290 --> 00:04:12.230
Recruiting members
 for the tennis team

00:04:10.740 --> 00:04:12.230
That's still going, too!

00:04:13.440 --> 00:04:16.270
What? Tell me more! In detail!

00:04:16.650 --> 00:04:19.880
You wouldn't expect it, but Kiki 
really likes that kind of thing.

00:04:19.880 --> 00:04:22.190
Come on! Tell me!

00:04:22.190 --> 00:04:23.320
Ow, ow, ow!

00:04:23.740 --> 00:04:25.010
All right.

00:04:25.010 --> 00:04:27.150
It's a plan suited to the 
moment. Let's run with it.

00:04:27.150 --> 00:04:28.880
We'll go with this for the next episode.

00:04:29.410 --> 00:04:31.370
Yes!

00:04:31.370 --> 00:04:32.240
Hey!

00:04:32.240 --> 00:04:34.850
You haven't told me anything yet!

00:04:32.240 --> 00:04:35.670
<i>And I did want to investigate 
Loveland High School, after all.</i>

00:04:42.800 --> 00:04:44.590
Business report for LFG CEO due

00:04:44.590 --> 00:04:45.930
Oh, no!

00:04:50.710 --> 00:04:51.590
please

00:04:53.560 --> 00:04:55.600
Okay! Just barely finished in time!

00:05:04.240 --> 00:05:05.420
<i>What?</i>

00:05:05.420 --> 00:05:10.350
I've just submitted our company's 
quarterly financial report to the auditor.

00:05:10.350 --> 00:05:14.120
I sent a copy to you, 
if you would look at it...

00:05:15.240 --> 00:05:19.160
<i>You called me in the middle of the night 
to tell me about your quarterly report?</i>

00:05:19.160 --> 00:05:20.680
The middle of the night?

00:05:22.440 --> 00:05:25.800
<b>Victor 
</b>I'll be in NY on business next week

00:05:23.420 --> 00:05:25.800
<i>I'll be in New York on business next week.</i>

00:05:33.320 --> 00:05:36.100
I-I'm so sorry! Goodnight!

00:05:44.230 --> 00:05:45.030
Yes?

00:05:45.680 --> 00:05:46.990
<i>You hung up on me.</i>

00:05:47.300 --> 00:05:51.720
No! I would never hang up on you, sir...

00:05:53.760 --> 00:05:55.330
I'm very sorry.

00:05:55.980 --> 00:05:57.070
Enough.

00:05:57.070 --> 00:05:59.510
I'll look at the report later. 
If there are issues,

00:05:59.510 --> 00:06:00.870
<i>I'll send a reply.</i>

00:06:00.870 --> 00:06:02.660
Oh, uh... yes, sir.

00:06:03.150 --> 00:06:04.020
<i>What?</i>

00:06:04.020 --> 00:06:06.840
Nothing. I just thought you'd 
be a lot angrier with me...

00:06:06.840 --> 00:06:10.800
Being angry with every little thing 
an idiot might do is a waste of time.

00:06:12.100 --> 00:06:13.890
<i>Is the show progressing smoothly?</i>

00:06:13.890 --> 00:06:15.050
Yes!

00:06:15.050 --> 00:06:17.560
I'm on my way to do some research 
at Loveland High School.

00:06:17.560 --> 00:06:18.770
Are you?

00:06:18.770 --> 00:06:21.860
Do be careful not to let your 
idiocy infect your underclassmen.

00:06:24.830 --> 00:06:26.270
If you'll excuse me!

00:06:29.610 --> 00:06:32.240
<b>Loveland High School</b>

00:06:29.610 --> 00:06:32.610
Oh, I know about that! 
A second-year girl, right?

00:06:32.610 --> 00:06:35.640
She suddenly stopped coming 
to school about six months ago,

00:06:35.640 --> 00:06:37.770
and they say she's gone missing!

00:06:37.770 --> 00:06:40.890
I heard she was always a little bit strange.

00:06:40.890 --> 00:06:43.290
Apparently, she didn't really have friends...

00:06:43.290 --> 00:06:46.520
And they say she had 
some kind of weird power.

00:06:47.180 --> 00:06:48.460
What's that supposed to mean?

00:06:48.460 --> 00:06:50.170
Teachers who were mean to her

00:06:50.170 --> 00:06:53.100
and upperclassmen in her club 
got hurt, one after another.

00:06:53.100 --> 00:06:56.110
Like, someone suddenly got burned, 
even though there wasn't any fire around!

00:06:56.110 --> 00:06:58.470
What? That doesn't make sense!

00:06:58.060 --> 00:07:00.020
Missing girl

00:06:58.060 --> 00:07:00.020
Loveland H.S.
 Interviews

00:07:03.460 --> 00:07:05.980
<i>Was she really taken by Black Swan, too?</i>

00:07:06.270 --> 00:07:09.320
Please! Won't you listen to my story?

00:07:09.320 --> 00:07:10.900
If you're from TV, I just know—

00:07:13.000 --> 00:07:14.190
That really got me hyped up.

00:07:14.190 --> 00:07:14.850
I know, right?

00:07:14.850 --> 00:07:15.600
Yeah.

00:07:17.380 --> 00:07:19.370
The disappearance of a second-year girl?

00:07:19.370 --> 00:07:21.220
Someone else just asked us about that.

00:07:21.220 --> 00:07:22.080
What?

00:07:22.080 --> 00:07:23.210
That guy there.

00:07:25.040 --> 00:07:26.400
Gavin-senpai?

00:07:27.950 --> 00:07:29.840
I see. You're here for research.

00:07:29.840 --> 00:07:34.380
Yes. Are you here about 
that student's disappearance?

00:07:35.500 --> 00:07:39.230
The fact that you're here means 
she really is an Evolver, right?

00:07:39.230 --> 00:07:43.280
Was she abducted by Black Swan,
 like that boy from before?

00:07:43.900 --> 00:07:47.750
What is Black Swan plotting, 
gathering up all these Evolvers?

00:07:48.300 --> 00:07:49.320
You...

00:07:49.320 --> 00:07:50.070
Yes?

00:07:50.690 --> 00:07:51.640
Huh?

00:07:51.640 --> 00:07:53.210
Your investigation comes first.

00:07:53.210 --> 00:07:53.880
What?

00:07:53.880 --> 00:07:55.490
W-Wait, Senpai!

00:07:55.490 --> 00:07:56.970
Senpai!

00:07:58.450 --> 00:08:04.330
<b>Lynn's Kitchen</b>

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:01.060
Um...

00:08:01.060 --> 00:08:04.330
Senpai, maybe you shouldn't
go into this restaurant?

00:08:04.620 --> 00:08:06.350
You want an interview, don't you?

00:08:06.350 --> 00:08:07.840
Yes, but...

00:08:13.950 --> 00:08:15.480
Wait, Senpai!

00:08:16.660 --> 00:08:18.360
Welcome!

00:08:23.420 --> 00:08:24.270
I'll have the usual.

00:08:26.140 --> 00:08:27.530
Of course.

00:08:32.840 --> 00:08:34.860
It really is still here!

00:08:35.410 --> 00:08:37.370
It hasn't changed at all!

00:08:40.440 --> 00:08:42.240
Thank you for waiting.

00:08:42.240 --> 00:08:46.510
Here's your beef ramen and a chashu ramen.

00:08:46.510 --> 00:08:48.590
Wow! This brings back memories!

00:08:49.200 --> 00:08:50.630
Let's eat!

00:09:02.780 --> 00:09:04.520
It's just like it used to be.

00:09:06.090 --> 00:09:07.270
Did you come here a lot?

00:09:07.590 --> 00:09:08.750
Yes.

00:09:08.750 --> 00:09:11.460
But the friend I used to come here with

00:09:11.460 --> 00:09:14.300
suddenly transferred schools 
at the end our first year,

00:09:14.300 --> 00:09:16.470
and I didn't have time to say goodbye...

00:09:20.700 --> 00:09:24.660
I might never see you again
And I didn't even get to say goodbye
I miss you

00:09:26.780 --> 00:09:28.170
After that, I didn't really...

00:09:29.180 --> 00:09:30.160
I see.

00:09:32.670 --> 00:09:33.840
Mr. Noah.

00:09:33.840 --> 00:09:34.670
Yes?

00:09:34.670 --> 00:09:38.800
We came here today because she says 
wants to do a story on this restaurant.

00:09:38.800 --> 00:09:40.970
A story?

00:09:40.970 --> 00:09:41.870
Yes!

00:09:42.260 --> 00:09:45.850
I'm a producer for a TV show,

00:09:45.850 --> 00:09:49.560
and I was hoping you'd allow me to do 
a story on this shop's message board.

00:09:49.560 --> 00:09:50.930
Oh!

00:09:50.930 --> 00:09:53.610
I'd have to talk to my wife about that.

00:09:53.610 --> 00:09:55.650
She's the one who started it, you see,

00:09:55.650 --> 00:09:58.030
and she doesn't like being in front of people.

00:09:58.300 --> 00:10:00.080
Would you do it as a favor?

00:10:00.920 --> 00:10:04.460
If it's a favor for you, 
Gavin-san, I can't say no...

00:10:04.460 --> 00:10:05.740
Senpai!

00:10:05.740 --> 00:10:08.550
I don't want to force them or anything...

00:10:12.320 --> 00:10:13.420
Give me just a second.

00:10:13.420 --> 00:10:14.390
Huh?

00:10:14.720 --> 00:10:16.080
Uh, okay.

00:10:18.540 --> 00:10:19.480
Here you are.

00:10:21.090 --> 00:10:22.920
I'll go talk to my wife.

00:10:22.920 --> 00:10:24.850
Please have these while you're waiting.

00:10:24.850 --> 00:10:26.990
Oh! You don't need to go 
to any trouble for me!

00:10:26.990 --> 00:10:29.600
I'm so sorry he's being so pushy.

00:10:29.600 --> 00:10:31.210
Don't worry about it.

00:10:31.210 --> 00:10:34.450
We owe Gavin-san quite a lot, you see.

00:10:35.820 --> 00:10:38.460
Um... Is this really all right?

00:10:38.460 --> 00:10:39.490
I'm sorry?

00:10:39.490 --> 00:10:43.330
He's not still threatening you 
after all this time, is he?!

00:10:49.280 --> 00:10:52.700
Gavin-san would never try 
to extort money out of us!

00:10:52.700 --> 00:10:53.720
B-But...

00:10:53.720 --> 00:10:58.010
I know I saw you pass Gavin-senpai 
an envelope full of money!

00:10:58.010 --> 00:11:02.320
Our family owes everything to Gavin-san.

00:11:10.520 --> 00:11:13.820
Gavin-san took our son 
to the hospital right away,

00:11:13.820 --> 00:11:16.220
and he even paid the medical fees.

00:11:16.220 --> 00:11:20.480
Thanks to him, our son was able to 
recover fully with no lasting effects.

00:11:20.480 --> 00:11:22.530
Then what I saw was...

00:11:23.280 --> 00:11:28.250
Gavin-san is someone who walks the path 
he believes in, no matter what others think.

00:11:28.250 --> 00:11:30.710
It seems a lot of people misunderstand him,

00:11:30.710 --> 00:11:34.000
but we are truly grateful to him.

00:11:37.150 --> 00:11:41.140
<i>If that's true, then what was 
that bloodstained letter about?</i>

00:11:43.610 --> 00:11:47.010
<b>Mr. Love: Queen's Choice</b>

00:11:48.680 --> 00:11:52.020
<b>Mr. Love: Queen's Choice</b>

00:12:01.410 --> 00:12:03.260
Were you able to gather enough information?

00:12:03.260 --> 00:12:05.640
Yes! Thank you for your help.

00:12:06.080 --> 00:12:07.790
If you're done, then hurry up and go home.

00:12:09.700 --> 00:12:12.450
But you're starting your own 
investigation now, right?

00:12:12.450 --> 00:12:13.510
I'll go, too!

00:12:13.510 --> 00:12:15.410
Headquarters contacted me earlier.

00:12:15.790 --> 00:12:18.130
It seems they've been active in this area.

00:12:18.460 --> 00:12:19.630
<i>Black Swan...</i>

00:12:19.630 --> 00:12:23.010
If you're with me, it's possible 
you'll get caught up in it.

00:12:23.010 --> 00:12:26.890
But I want to know what 
they're up to! So I'll go—

00:12:26.890 --> 00:12:30.100
I told you. Your life may be put at risk.

00:12:35.100 --> 00:12:38.730
If I find anything out, 
I'll be sure to tell you later.

00:12:38.730 --> 00:12:40.520
Just go home for today.

00:12:50.120 --> 00:12:51.870
Minor

00:12:53.900 --> 00:12:55.750
Minor? Is something wrong?

00:12:55.750 --> 00:12:57.210
<i>Is the research going well?</i>

00:12:57.570 --> 00:13:01.380
So what was it like being back 
at your old school after so long?

00:13:01.380 --> 00:13:03.470
Did it make you remember anything?

00:13:04.310 --> 00:13:05.550
"Anything," meaning?

00:13:05.550 --> 00:13:07.700
Oh, come on, you know.

00:13:07.700 --> 00:13:10.940
Memories from high school, 
like about heartbreak, or promises,

00:13:10.940 --> 00:13:14.020
or letters secretly placed in your desk...

00:13:14.820 --> 00:13:16.480
How do you know about that?!

00:13:16.480 --> 00:13:17.320
Huh?

00:13:17.320 --> 00:13:21.510
Well, you know, a lot of 
things happened, and...

00:13:21.900 --> 00:13:23.040
Minor!

00:13:23.040 --> 00:13:25.600
<i>Now, now. Don't sweat the little things.</i>

00:13:25.600 --> 00:13:27.240
<i>How did the research go?</i>

00:13:31.900 --> 00:13:33.200
<i>Hello?</i>

00:13:33.200 --> 00:13:34.910
<i>President, can you hear me?</i>

00:13:34.910 --> 00:13:36.290
Sorry. I'll call you later.

00:13:36.290 --> 00:13:37.260
<i>Huh? Pres—</i>

00:13:42.930 --> 00:13:44.800
I have to tell Senpai...

00:14:33.100 --> 00:14:36.620
That's not going to 
break you free of my sand.

00:14:40.500 --> 00:14:41.350
Stop it!

00:14:45.210 --> 00:14:47.210
What do you get out of doing this?

00:14:47.690 --> 00:14:49.740
What are all of you after?

00:14:49.740 --> 00:14:51.520
Who knows?

00:14:51.520 --> 00:14:56.130
All I've been told is that I need
to throw you off this roof.

00:14:59.010 --> 00:15:01.000
<i>He took off my bracelet?</i>

00:15:01.000 --> 00:15:03.540
<i>No, even so, Senpai will...</i>

00:15:03.540 --> 00:15:05.210
The police will be here soon.

00:15:05.210 --> 00:15:06.870
Sounds good.

00:15:08.270 --> 00:15:12.120
We'll have them pick up your corpse.

00:15:13.640 --> 00:15:17.460
Sorry. I've got nothing against you personally.

00:15:17.460 --> 00:15:19.310
This is for my little sister.

00:15:24.080 --> 00:15:25.740
Playing tricks, are you?!

00:15:26.220 --> 00:15:27.350
Die!

00:15:28.080 --> 00:15:31.780
As long as you are somewhere 
in the wind, I will always find you.

00:15:32.140 --> 00:15:33.240
<i>Gavin-senpai!</i>

00:15:42.830 --> 00:15:45.100
What is this? My power...

00:15:45.840 --> 00:15:47.400
I can't hold it—

00:16:17.610 --> 00:16:19.180
Gavin-senpai!

00:16:19.180 --> 00:16:20.580
You're all right now.

00:16:21.260 --> 00:16:22.540
But that's...

00:16:32.940 --> 00:16:34.290
It came loose...

00:16:36.640 --> 00:16:38.100
Senpai, behind you!

00:16:40.660 --> 00:16:41.840
Hang on!

00:16:51.480 --> 00:16:53.250
Backup will be here soon.

00:16:53.250 --> 00:16:54.780
No need to worry about the rest.

00:17:09.910 --> 00:17:11.170
Serves you right!

00:17:11.460 --> 00:17:14.610
Aren't you gonna finish him off, Senpai?

00:17:14.610 --> 00:17:17.140
You need to learn your place, kid!

00:17:17.140 --> 00:17:19.040
If you've learned your lesson, you'd better—

00:17:19.040 --> 00:17:20.120
I don't...

00:17:21.150 --> 00:17:23.400
I don't take orders from anyone!

00:17:24.730 --> 00:17:25.980
Take this!

00:17:29.500 --> 00:17:30.980
Die already!

00:17:45.520 --> 00:17:46.770
<i>No!</i>

00:17:46.770 --> 00:17:48.080
<i>I still...</i>

00:18:03.070 --> 00:18:05.730
<i>You gave me life.</i>

00:18:05.730 --> 00:18:09.340
<i>That's why I will risk 
everything to protect you.</i>

00:18:12.410 --> 00:18:13.740
Don't lose it again.

00:18:13.740 --> 00:18:14.660
I won't.

00:18:16.890 --> 00:18:20.310
Senpai, how did you know I was on the roof?

00:18:20.310 --> 00:18:22.120
I didn't have this GPS tracker with me.

00:18:22.120 --> 00:18:26.160
I told you. As long as you're in 
the wind, I will always find you.

00:18:27.660 --> 00:18:29.820
Wait, then what is this for?

00:18:31.050 --> 00:18:34.090
The next time you call for me, 
don't call me "Senpai."

00:18:34.090 --> 00:18:35.560
Call me Gavin.

00:18:37.520 --> 00:18:38.340
I will.

00:18:42.350 --> 00:18:43.920
<i>A week later,</i>

00:18:43.920 --> 00:18:45.540
<i>I received a report.</i>

00:18:46.100 --> 00:18:50.230
<i>The person who attacked me, 
Jay, had a younger twin sister.</i>

00:18:46.910 --> 00:18:50.230
Could you make this section
a little more compact?

00:18:50.490 --> 00:18:53.190
<i>Because she had a very strong Evol,</i>

00:18:53.190 --> 00:18:55.730
<i>she was being held captive 
at the center of Black Swan.</i>

00:18:56.170 --> 00:19:00.200
<i>Jay had attacked me 
in exchange for his sister.</i>

00:19:01.120 --> 00:19:04.660
<i>And these siblings, Jay and
 his younger sister Josie,</i>

00:19:04.660 --> 00:19:07.180
<i>were named in the last case 
my father had worked on,</i>

00:19:07.180 --> 00:19:09.690
<i>the disappearance of a family 
in north Loveland City.</i>

00:19:09.690 --> 00:19:11.530
<i>They were the children who'd vanished.</i>

00:19:12.670 --> 00:19:16.000
<i>My father's death, the memories 
I just can't recall...</i>

00:19:16.860 --> 00:19:19.050
<i>Everything is connected</i>

00:19:19.050 --> 00:19:22.970
<i>to Black Swan's dark conspiracy.</i>

00:19:24.940 --> 00:19:27.970
Thank you for sending the 
report on your investigation.

00:19:27.970 --> 00:19:31.750
I still don't know why 
Black Swan is targeting you.

00:19:31.750 --> 00:19:32.880
Be careful.

00:19:32.880 --> 00:19:33.810
<i>I will.</i>

00:19:35.680 --> 00:19:37.240
Minor told me something.

00:19:37.240 --> 00:19:41.400
He said, "Back then, my big bro Gavin 
asked me to put the letter in your desk."

00:19:42.370 --> 00:19:43.450
<i>I'm so sorry.</i>

00:19:43.450 --> 00:19:46.470
<i>I assumed it was some kind of threat...</i>

00:19:46.470 --> 00:19:49.190
<i>What did you write in the letter?</i>

00:19:51.120 --> 00:19:53.370
I might never see you again
And I didn't even get to say goodbye
I miss you

00:19:52.600 --> 00:19:55.840
So this... just needs 
to go in her desk, right?

00:19:55.840 --> 00:19:58.210
Whoa... It's covered in blood...

00:19:58.720 --> 00:20:00.870
I messed up during training.

00:20:01.370 --> 00:20:04.090
Sorry to ask, but rewrite it for me, okay?

00:20:04.090 --> 00:20:06.600
I don't think I'll have time before I enlist.

00:20:07.120 --> 00:20:09.970
This is pretty cool in its own way, though...

00:20:11.000 --> 00:20:14.350
I bet you were flipping out over what 
to write up until the last second.

00:20:14.350 --> 00:20:16.670
Whoa! That was close!

00:20:18.800 --> 00:20:20.840
I accept the mission!

00:20:20.840 --> 00:20:24.800
I promise, my bro Gavin's 
feelings will be delivered!

00:20:28.220 --> 00:20:30.610
Let's leave that letter in the past.

00:20:30.990 --> 00:20:33.820
We still have the future, after all.

00:22:06.460 --> 00:22:09.840
We've confirmed that 
they did have a base here.

00:22:10.160 --> 00:22:12.980
Brokers involved in that 
incident seventeen years ago,

00:22:12.980 --> 00:22:15.220
and an organization tied to moneylending.

00:22:15.810 --> 00:22:19.450
Seems like quite a few of the big players 
in the financial world are connected, too.

00:22:21.240 --> 00:22:23.260
It was just three days ago.

00:22:23.260 --> 00:22:27.070
It's being made to look like
 a gas explosion to the public.

00:22:27.580 --> 00:22:29.590
Here's the report on everything so far.

00:22:32.720 --> 00:22:34.510
What about that girl?

00:22:35.000 --> 00:22:38.100
Thought you said you'd 
found a likely candidate.

00:22:38.620 --> 00:22:40.730
There's no concrete evidence yet.

00:22:40.730 --> 00:22:45.450
If the reason for her missing memories 
lies in the incident seventeen years ago,

00:22:45.450 --> 00:22:47.730
the wrong approach would 
be counterproductive.

00:22:48.320 --> 00:22:51.230
You mean PTSD?

00:22:51.230 --> 00:22:53.730
In that case, all you can do
 is proceed with caution.

00:22:59.580 --> 00:23:00.440
Look out!

00:23:01.440 --> 00:23:04.150
I will get it back,

00:23:04.150 --> 00:23:06.390
no matter the cost.

00:23:21.120 --> 00:23:25.000
<i>A beautiful sight that brings 
feelings of nostalgia...</i>

00:23:25.000 --> 00:23:28.340
<i>If you relax into the swaying 
memories in the shade of this tree,</i>

00:23:28.340 --> 00:23:30.390
<i>you'll start to see who you really are.</i>

00:23:30.390 --> 00:23:31.550
<i>Episode six...</i>

00:23:31.550 --> 00:23:33.200
<i>"Beyond That Dream."</i>

00:23:31.550 --> 00:23:34.960
"Beyond That Dream"
